# CoralStack oMLX runtime config for the Mac mini.
#
# install.sh copies this to ~/.coralstack/omlx.env on the box. That copy is
# LOCAL AND UNTRACKED — it holds the API key. Same pattern as
# ~/.coralstack/ollama.env beside it and the gitignored services/*/.env files on
# the apps VM: the repo carries the shape, the box carries the secret.
#
# omlx-serve.sh sources this file and EXPORTS the key rather than passing it as
# a flag, which matters: a command line is visible to every local user through
# `ps`, while a process environment is readable only by its owner and root. The
# LaunchAgent plist does not carry the key either, so it never lands in
# ~/Library/LaunchAgents.

# The server's API key. oMLX REFUSES to bind anything but loopback without one,
# which is the single way this is already better than the Ollama it replaces:
# Ollama listens on 0.0.0.0:11434 with no authentication whatsoever.
#
# install.sh generates one with `openssl rand -hex 32` if this is blank, and
# prints it once. The same value has to reach two other places BY HAND, and
# nothing detects a mismatch except a 401:
#   - services/open-webui/.env on the apps VM, as OMLX_API_KEY
#   - the Perennial client's own config, in its own repo
OMLX_API_KEY=

# Where the model snapshots live. One directory per `org/name` from
# omlx-models.txt — oMLX supports that two-level layout natively.
OMLX_MODEL_DIR=

# The paged SSD cache. THIS IS THE FEATURE, so its sizing is declared rather
# than defaulted — but SIZE IT FOR THE CONTEXT LENGTH YOU ACTUALLY WANT.
#
# Measured 2026-10-16: two 46k-token conversations occupied 15 GB, i.e. ~7.5 GB
# each, or ~163 KB per token. Extrapolated to the 230k contexts this box is now
# configured for, that is ~37 GB for ONE conversation — so the 40 GB this file
# used to carry held exactly one, and the agents need at least two.
#
# 300 GB against 790 GB free is ~8 conversations at 230k. Note this value
# OVERRIDES the default in omlx-serve.sh, which is how a 40 GB value here
# silently defeated a 300 GB default in the repo; if you are wondering why a
# flag change did not take, check this file first.
OMLX_SSD_CACHE_DIR=
OMLX_SSD_CACHE_MAX_SIZE=300GB

# The in-RAM tier for INACTIVE conversations. Small on purpose — it competes
# with the active context, and the SSD tier is only ~0.1s slower. See the long
# comment in omlx-serve.sh. Blank uses the wrapper's default of 1GB.
OMLX_HOT_CACHE_MAX_SIZE=

# Gated DeltaNet state storage. These have NO CLI FLAG — omlx-serve.sh merges
# them into ~/.omlx/settings.json before starting the server, because the server
# rewrites that file on every startup and anything set there by hand is
# undeclared state waiting to be lost.
#
# Precision: fp32|bf16|int8|rht_int8|rht_int16. Storage:
# auto|ssd_sidecar|embedded, and the codec ONLY applies on the sidecar path, so
# a codec with `auto` may quietly do nothing.
#
# Blank uses the wrapper's defaults, rht_int8 / ssd_sidecar, which were
# measured on this box against upstream's fp32 default: SSD footprint halved
# (15 GB -> 7.5 GB for two 46k conversations), switch time unchanged at 1s,
# restart faster at 4s against 6s, cold prefill within 1%.
OMLX_GDN_PRECISION=
OMLX_GDN_STORAGE=
